WEBVTT

00:00:10.480 --> 00:00:12.490
You're still sleeping?

00:00:23.060 --> 00:00:24.170
Mom?

00:00:27.620 --> 00:00:28.290
Dad?

00:00:28.290 --> 00:00:30.670
Oh, you're finally up.

00:00:31.070 --> 00:00:34.270
You'd better get ready or we'll be late.

00:00:34.270 --> 00:00:35.930
Late?

00:00:35.930 --> 00:00:38.310
It was your idea, Ayase!

00:00:38.310 --> 00:00:40.160
You wanted us to take you on a picnic.

00:00:40.160 --> 00:00:42.180
Hurry up and eat.

00:00:43.560 --> 00:00:45.360
Have you forgotten?

00:00:46.530 --> 00:00:47.810
No.

00:00:48.260 --> 00:00:49.450
That's right.

00:00:49.450 --> 00:00:52.680
I wanted to go on a picnic...

00:00:53.800 --> 00:00:56.070
with my mom and dad!

00:01:13.440 --> 00:01:15.010
Get on, kid.

00:01:15.400 --> 00:01:17.010
We're gonna save Ayase.

00:01:17.880 --> 00:01:19.090
Wait.

00:01:19.090 --> 00:01:20.540
We can't attack without knowing...

00:01:20.540 --> 00:01:22.050
I know where to strike.

00:01:24.120 --> 00:01:26.810
Audium's real body is that mask.

00:01:26.810 --> 00:01:29.470
Then if we destroy the mask...

00:01:29.470 --> 00:01:31.570
Ayase will be released.

00:01:31.570 --> 00:01:33.950
But it won't be that easy.

00:01:33.950 --> 00:01:37.570
If you approach carelessly, 
she might steal your resources.

00:01:37.570 --> 00:01:41.080
But I can't just stand here and watch!

00:01:41.630 --> 00:01:43.210
You're right, Rigel.

00:01:43.210 --> 00:01:44.910
We don't have a moment to spare.

00:01:46.960 --> 00:01:50.920
Sieger, I'll help you.

00:01:51.260 --> 00:01:55.170
Then I will open a path.

00:01:55.170 --> 00:01:57.550
We'll go, too! Tyranno!

00:01:58.610 --> 00:01:59.640
Okay!

00:02:03.320 --> 00:02:06.890
Tennoji, please save Ayase!

00:02:09.030 --> 00:02:12.400
<i>Ayase, you're keeping your promise to me.</i>

00:02:12.400 --> 00:02:15.030
<i>Your life is mine.</i>

00:02:15.620 --> 00:02:18.530
<i>I'm not letting that thing take it.</i>

00:02:18.530 --> 00:02:23.030
<i>You're coming back to me, Ayase!</i>

00:02:24.940 --> 00:02:26.540
What's wrong?

00:02:27.800 --> 00:02:31.530
It felt like somebody was calling my name.

00:02:31.530 --> 00:02:32.920
You were hearing things.

00:02:33.410 --> 00:02:35.300
You... think so?

00:02:39.110 --> 00:02:41.450
Let's eat at the top of that hill.

00:02:41.450 --> 00:02:42.430
Let's go.

00:02:44.390 --> 00:02:45.430
Yeah.

00:03:19.720 --> 00:03:20.970
Rindo!

00:03:35.960 --> 00:03:38.360
Angle of inclination: +3 degrees.

00:03:39.360 --> 00:03:40.400
Shoot!

00:03:55.240 --> 00:03:56.210
There's no end to them!

00:03:56.630 --> 00:03:57.960
Tyranno!

00:03:58.490 --> 00:04:00.240
We're at full power!

00:04:00.240 --> 00:04:01.720
Go!

00:04:05.860 --> 00:04:08.550
Nice job, stone reptile boy!

00:04:08.550 --> 00:04:11.850
Let's go! Sieger! Fierte!

00:04:23.200 --> 00:04:24.990
That doesn't suit you.

00:04:25.860 --> 00:04:27.200
Merely a whim.

00:04:27.880 --> 00:04:29.700
No time to be looking around, kid!

00:04:30.180 --> 00:04:31.120
Yeah!

00:04:36.920 --> 00:04:38.290
Here it comes!

00:04:45.970 --> 00:04:47.400
Tennoji...

00:04:54.900 --> 00:04:55.920
Fierte!

00:04:55.920 --> 00:04:58.250
Audium is absorbing her resources!

00:04:58.250 --> 00:04:59.060
What?

00:05:01.570 --> 00:05:04.820
If she needs resources, I've got them!

00:05:05.250 --> 00:05:07.150
Don't push your limits!

00:05:07.150 --> 00:05:10.580
Your body is under a lot of strain as it is.

00:05:10.930 --> 00:05:11.880
It's fine.

00:05:11.880 --> 00:05:20.590
Right now, this is all I can do 
for you, Sieger, and Ayase!

00:05:21.600 --> 00:05:23.090
Asuka...

00:05:23.890 --> 00:05:25.670
<i>He's a pretty impressive kid.</i>

00:05:26.090 --> 00:05:27.120
<i>But...</i>

00:05:28.150 --> 00:05:32.170
<i>It looks like I need you after all.</i>

00:05:33.100 --> 00:05:34.220
<i>Ayase...</i>

00:05:35.850 --> 00:05:38.000
<i>I'm embarrassed to ask this,</i>

00:05:38.000 --> 00:05:40.300
<i>but can you help us out?</i>

00:05:40.300 --> 00:05:43.390
<i>I'll pay you back by sleeping 
next to you tonight.</i>

00:05:43.390 --> 00:05:45.110
I'd rather you didn't!

00:05:47.030 --> 00:05:48.180
Ayase?

00:05:48.180 --> 00:05:49.370
What's wrong?

00:06:06.720 --> 00:06:07.950
Oh, yeah...

00:06:09.710 --> 00:06:11.310
That's right...

00:06:16.100 --> 00:06:17.830
Mom and Dad...

00:06:22.260 --> 00:06:23.980
died, didn't they?

00:06:25.750 --> 00:06:26.860
Right here.

00:06:33.010 --> 00:06:34.180
Ayase...

00:06:34.180 --> 00:06:35.320
Ayase...

00:06:43.190 --> 00:06:47.510
Goodbye, Mom, Dad.

00:06:47.510 --> 00:06:50.460
The picnic was fun.

00:06:57.970 --> 00:06:58.810
It came loose?

00:07:00.800 --> 00:07:02.730
Did you hear that, Ayase?

00:07:04.310 --> 00:07:05.850
Take this, kid!

00:07:07.030 --> 00:07:09.100
Audium's stopped moving.

00:07:09.100 --> 00:07:10.950
This is our only chance!

00:07:10.950 --> 00:07:12.570
Get ready!

00:07:20.420 --> 00:07:21.330
Go!

00:07:24.000 --> 00:07:25.600
What's wrong, kid?

00:07:26.520 --> 00:07:27.340
I really...

00:07:27.340 --> 00:07:28.340
Asuka!

00:07:29.000 --> 00:07:30.340
...hate...

00:07:30.340 --> 00:07:31.590
Get going!

00:07:31.590 --> 00:07:34.240
...heights!

00:07:35.500 --> 00:07:36.970
I'll do it!

00:07:39.960 --> 00:07:43.730
I'm here to save you, Ayase!

00:07:51.370 --> 00:07:54.140
<i>Ayase, you can see him, can't you?</i>

00:07:54.140 --> 00:07:57.490
<i>There... The person you care about.</i>

00:08:11.140 --> 00:08:12.600
Curse you!

00:08:17.600 --> 00:08:18.890
Asuka!

00:08:28.140 --> 00:08:32.150
Curse you! Curse you! Curse you!

00:08:44.500 --> 00:08:45.400
Asuka!

00:08:45.970 --> 00:08:47.180
Where's Asuka?

00:08:48.450 --> 00:08:49.920
Over there.

00:08:50.380 --> 00:08:53.010
No!

00:08:53.010 --> 00:08:56.880
I'm falling! I'm falling!

00:08:54.540 --> 00:08:56.880
Hey, don't cling to me like that!

00:09:04.160 --> 00:09:06.810
W-We're saved.

00:09:08.710 --> 00:09:10.400
Will you get off me already?!

00:09:11.710 --> 00:09:16.190
N-N-No!

00:09:18.280 --> 00:09:20.670
Are you all right, Asuka?

00:09:21.980 --> 00:09:24.790
Fierte!

00:09:39.250 --> 00:09:40.220
Ayase!

00:09:43.730 --> 00:09:45.330
I'm sorry!

00:09:45.840 --> 00:09:49.070
It's my fault that happened to you...

00:09:51.960 --> 00:09:53.480
Thank you, Aina.

00:09:54.920 --> 00:09:57.590
I heard your voice.

00:09:57.590 --> 00:10:00.360
That's why I was able to come back.

00:10:00.360 --> 00:10:03.130
So we're square now.

00:10:03.130 --> 00:10:04.270
We're even.

00:10:05.290 --> 00:10:06.600
Ayase...

00:10:10.000 --> 00:10:13.630
Now you don't need to harm Kobe, right?

00:10:15.790 --> 00:10:16.880
Of course.

00:10:19.970 --> 00:10:21.960
You really broke it.

00:10:21.960 --> 00:10:23.640
What a waste.

00:10:24.280 --> 00:10:25.390
You're...

00:10:28.390 --> 00:10:30.120
Gambiel!

00:10:32.110 --> 00:10:33.140
I'll never forgive you!

00:10:35.110 --> 00:10:36.440
Never!

00:10:37.040 --> 00:10:39.400
You'll never forgive me?

00:10:39.400 --> 00:10:43.950
Then you should've just 
let Audium swallow you.

00:10:43.950 --> 00:10:47.910
You could've killed all the angels, 
just like you wanted.

00:10:47.910 --> 00:10:50.080
What an idiot!

00:10:54.270 --> 00:10:55.900
You're the idiot.

00:10:55.900 --> 00:10:58.220
That's not what Ayase wants.

00:11:02.480 --> 00:11:06.410
You want to die that badly, huh?

00:11:16.420 --> 00:11:17.570
Who's there?

00:11:23.070 --> 00:11:24.520
Gambiel.

00:11:24.520 --> 00:11:26.700
I will not allow you to act willfully any longer.

00:11:26.700 --> 00:11:28.340
You won't allow it?

00:11:28.340 --> 00:11:32.210
I don't think you've got any 
right to tell me that, Michael.

00:11:32.680 --> 00:11:35.210
This is Uriel's order.

00:11:35.210 --> 00:11:36.860
U-Uriel's order?

00:11:36.860 --> 00:11:38.350
He's back?

00:11:38.350 --> 00:11:42.130
Yes. And I have many questions to ask you.

00:11:42.130 --> 00:11:43.720
Return immediately.

00:11:43.720 --> 00:11:45.230
Sure thing!

00:11:45.230 --> 00:11:47.220
Right, Gambiel?

00:11:50.130 --> 00:11:53.980
Hmph. There's no way I can win 
against the four archangels.

00:11:53.980 --> 00:11:56.480
Fine, I'll go home.

00:11:56.480 --> 00:11:57.350
Let's do that!

00:11:57.350 --> 00:11:58.570
Yeah, let's do that!

00:11:58.570 --> 00:11:59.480
Wait!

00:11:59.800 --> 00:12:01.380
Bye!

00:12:01.380 --> 00:12:02.530
Sieger!

00:12:02.530 --> 00:12:03.980
Sister Ayase...

00:12:06.120 --> 00:12:09.320
So you were the Angel Killer, then?

00:12:11.720 --> 00:12:13.500
Sakura?

00:12:15.030 --> 00:12:18.060
If you're going to continue to hunt angels,

00:12:18.060 --> 00:12:20.350
then I will be your next opponent.

00:12:32.260 --> 00:12:33.290
Fierte...

00:12:33.780 --> 00:12:34.770
Yes?

00:12:35.110 --> 00:12:37.520
You still don't wish to return?

00:12:39.520 --> 00:12:45.990
With Uriel back, we angels will 
strive to coexist with humanity.

00:12:46.690 --> 00:12:47.780
Yes.

00:12:48.180 --> 00:12:51.040
Will you remain here regardless?

00:12:51.940 --> 00:12:53.300
I...

00:13:00.850 --> 00:13:03.550
Do what you want to do.

00:13:07.500 --> 00:13:09.610
I will remain here.

00:13:10.880 --> 00:13:12.410
Very well.

00:13:12.410 --> 00:13:15.810
I will tell that to Uriel.

00:13:16.600 --> 00:13:18.040
Asuka Tennoji...

00:13:18.810 --> 00:13:20.790
Take care of Fierte.

00:13:21.840 --> 00:13:23.320
Leave it to me!

00:13:23.320 --> 00:13:26.200
Uh, how do you know my name?

00:13:34.200 --> 00:13:41.210
I didn't expect Uriel to reveal himself so soon.

00:13:41.610 --> 00:13:45.680
We'll have to stay put for a while, Gabriel.

00:13:45.680 --> 00:13:48.160
I don't need to hear that from you!

00:13:49.970 --> 00:13:52.390
So that's the second one...

00:13:52.980 --> 00:13:56.100
I'm sure they'll come in handy someday.

00:13:58.010 --> 00:14:06.430
Until then, enjoy your time in 
the sun to its fullest, Uriel.

00:14:12.390 --> 00:14:16.500
The word "retreat" is not in my vocabulary.

00:14:16.920 --> 00:14:18.500
Don't get the wrong idea.

00:14:18.500 --> 00:14:20.000
This isn't a retreat.

00:14:20.000 --> 00:14:23.070
Then what is it?

00:14:23.070 --> 00:14:27.510
We're just heading to a supply 
base to reorganize our troops.

00:14:29.510 --> 00:14:33.100
We can't be certain that we won't 
run into an enemy like Audium

00:14:33.100 --> 00:14:35.870
and have our advance stopped again.

00:14:35.870 --> 00:14:42.520
To avoid that, we need to enhance our 
forces and reevaluate our invasion plans.

00:14:44.470 --> 00:14:46.530
It's not a retreat, then?

00:14:47.140 --> 00:14:47.780
It's not.

00:14:48.150 --> 00:14:49.950
Very well!

00:14:52.740 --> 00:14:54.030
Mikado!

00:14:57.640 --> 00:14:58.500
Are you going?

00:14:58.500 --> 00:14:59.230
Yeah.

00:14:59.230 --> 00:15:02.790
I want to get to Nagoya as soon as possible.

00:15:03.460 --> 00:15:06.550
Don't cry when I'm gone, okay?

00:15:07.800 --> 00:15:09.800
I hope you find your mother.

00:15:09.800 --> 00:15:13.300
And I hope you find the person 
you're looking for, too.

00:15:19.630 --> 00:15:21.080
She knew, huh?

00:15:26.070 --> 00:15:28.570
Are you sure you don't 
want to say goodbye?

00:15:28.570 --> 00:15:30.070
I'll see them again.

00:15:30.410 --> 00:15:31.680
You're right.

00:15:31.680 --> 00:15:33.190
We're going to get moving.

00:15:33.190 --> 00:15:35.990
Is it okay for you to go back to Tohoku?

00:15:35.990 --> 00:15:37.740
You deserted, didn't you?

00:15:37.740 --> 00:15:39.840
Those guys can't be bothered to do anything.

00:15:39.840 --> 00:15:42.040
They won't find me.

00:15:42.040 --> 00:15:43.630
What about you, Rigel?

00:15:44.190 --> 00:15:47.230
It'll be easier to avoid the 
Administrators in a place that's

00:15:47.230 --> 00:15:51.320
under the control of another world, 
so it's actually better for me.

00:15:52.310 --> 00:15:56.950
Plus, there's a chance we 
can heal Azumi's illness.

00:15:57.670 --> 00:15:59.780
I'll go wherever I have to.

00:16:03.140 --> 00:16:08.650
I promise I'll take Azumi to 
the Eight Great Dragon Kings.

00:16:09.200 --> 00:16:10.570
Thanks.

00:16:10.570 --> 00:16:14.230
Okay, let's get going to Tohoku!

00:16:25.110 --> 00:16:27.040
Take care out there.

00:16:28.030 --> 00:16:28.760
Yeah.

00:16:29.310 --> 00:16:30.990
Come visit once in a while.

00:16:31.520 --> 00:16:32.360
Yeah.

00:16:34.070 --> 00:16:36.720
Um, Tennoji...

00:16:37.190 --> 00:16:38.220
What?

00:16:39.090 --> 00:16:40.270
I...

00:16:42.510 --> 00:16:44.230
I like you, Tennoji!

00:16:45.240 --> 00:16:47.530
I like you too, Aina!

00:16:47.530 --> 00:16:48.980
We're friends, after all!

00:16:51.030 --> 00:16:53.240
That's just like you.

00:17:00.360 --> 00:17:01.370
Seriously...

00:17:02.240 --> 00:17:03.870
He's so dense.

00:17:06.830 --> 00:17:10.720
How're you doing, everybody?

00:17:10.720 --> 00:17:12.550
It's me, Misaki Yuzuriha!

00:17:13.800 --> 00:17:16.290
Stop looking at my chest!

00:17:16.290 --> 00:17:20.520
Boys who look at girls that 
way need to be punished.

00:17:24.180 --> 00:17:25.100
Number Withheld

00:17:26.470 --> 00:17:27.950
Is that Ayase?

00:17:27.950 --> 00:17:28.810
Yes?

00:17:28.810 --> 00:17:30.070
Hello?

00:17:34.400 --> 00:17:35.970
You're leaving too, huh?

00:17:35.970 --> 00:17:36.820
Yes.

00:17:36.820 --> 00:17:39.920
What will you do now?

00:17:39.920 --> 00:17:44.600
I'm going back to Yokohama 
to think about what to do next.

00:17:44.600 --> 00:17:45.630
I see.

00:17:51.760 --> 00:17:53.340
So...

00:17:55.500 --> 00:17:58.300
B-Before that...

00:17:58.300 --> 00:17:59.780
I wanted to tell you...

00:17:59.780 --> 00:18:01.030
What?

00:18:01.560 --> 00:18:02.640
Nothing!

00:18:03.850 --> 00:18:05.570
What was that about?

00:18:12.420 --> 00:18:13.750
What's with them?

00:18:13.750 --> 00:18:14.890
I don't know.

00:18:21.680 --> 00:18:22.710
Who's that?

00:18:23.230 --> 00:18:24.330
Hello?

00:18:25.250 --> 00:18:28.960
I wanted to tell you this:

00:18:35.590 --> 00:18:36.710
Thank you.

00:18:38.360 --> 00:18:40.590
Just can't be honest with yourself...

00:18:43.670 --> 00:18:46.130
Everybody's gone.

00:18:46.130 --> 00:18:48.630
It's kind of lonely.

00:18:50.440 --> 00:18:52.110
Don't worry.

00:18:53.110 --> 00:18:54.560
We'll see them again.

00:19:00.240 --> 00:19:03.740
By the way, I got a call 
from Yamato yesterday.

00:19:03.740 --> 00:19:05.080
From my brother?

00:19:05.080 --> 00:19:06.080
What did he say?

00:19:06.080 --> 00:19:08.470
He's coming back to Japan soon.

00:19:08.470 --> 00:19:11.440
Yamato Tennoji

00:19:08.810 --> 00:19:10.250
Really?

00:19:12.620 --> 00:19:16.400
He said he's going to check and see 
if you're getting by on your own.

00:19:16.400 --> 00:19:17.970
What's that supposed to mean?

00:19:17.970 --> 00:19:20.630
I haven't seen him in a long time, though.

00:19:20.630 --> 00:19:23.670
I told him you have a girlfriend.

00:19:25.930 --> 00:19:27.370
Ow! Hot!

00:19:27.370 --> 00:19:29.740
Are you okay?

00:19:28.150 --> 00:19:30.390
Honestly...

00:19:30.390 --> 00:19:32.830
You really are hopeless.

00:19:36.110 --> 00:19:38.820
The danger has passed, it seems.

00:19:38.820 --> 00:19:42.810
It was a great danger to them,

00:19:42.810 --> 00:19:46.830
but just a minor incident 
to the rest of the world.

00:19:46.830 --> 00:19:48.670
That's right.

00:19:48.670 --> 00:19:53.870
They have not escaped from their fate yet.

00:19:54.480 --> 00:19:57.470
At this rate, the world will be destroyed.

00:19:57.920 --> 00:20:02.040
Be it red, blue, white, black, or green...

00:20:02.960 --> 00:20:05.850
whichever future we choose.

00:20:06.430 --> 00:20:09.440
We need a sixth future.

00:20:09.440 --> 00:20:14.010
But all we can do is sow the seeds.

00:20:17.560 --> 00:20:24.370
Perhaps that boy can show us the path.

00:20:27.140 --> 00:20:28.640
Spring is at hand.

00:20:29.200 --> 00:20:31.600
The seeds are beginning to sprout.

00:20:34.900 --> 00:20:38.720
One day, they will bloom into brilliant flowers,

00:20:39.330 --> 00:20:41.900
or grow into great, strong trees.

00:20:42.700 --> 00:20:47.490
We need only wait quietly and 
see what becomes of them.

00:20:50.180 --> 00:20:52.640
It was so busy today.

00:20:52.640 --> 00:20:54.640
You must be tired.

00:20:54.980 --> 00:20:58.150
I'm sure it's harder with Aina gone.

00:20:58.150 --> 00:21:00.290
School's finally about to start, too.

00:21:00.290 --> 00:21:02.740
I'll need to find a new job.

00:21:02.740 --> 00:21:06.410
Um, do you think I could do it?

00:21:07.640 --> 00:21:09.160
You?

00:21:09.590 --> 00:21:14.030
Well, I don't want to make you 
do everything for me all the time.

00:21:14.710 --> 00:21:16.420
Could I?

00:21:16.420 --> 00:21:17.670
Why not?

00:21:18.310 --> 00:21:20.920
I'll talk to the boss tomorrow.

00:21:22.820 --> 00:21:23.830
Okay!

00:21:28.880 --> 00:21:30.120
Snow?

00:21:31.170 --> 00:21:33.190
No wonder I was cold.

00:21:33.190 --> 00:21:35.690
Let's get home, Fierte.

00:21:35.690 --> 00:21:36.670
Yeah.

00:21:46.720 --> 00:21:50.280
Shall we go, Uriel?

00:23:27.520 --> 00:23:29.280
This smells so good!

00:23:29.280 --> 00:23:32.430
Your coffee is the best in the world.

00:23:35.490 --> 00:23:38.020
I know you're flattering me, 
but it still makes me happy.

